# ADU bytes: the 7 byte MBAP header (transaction id, protocol id, length, unit id), then the PDU.
# Serialized by the S04b adapter (crates/stonecrab/tests/modbus_driver_suite_adapter.rs) from the XML model of the step "unnamed outgoing-plc-message at position 3" of test case "85 Query: Trans: 28; Unit: 1, Func: 16: Write Multiple Registers" in fixtures/modbus/upstream/tcp/Modbus-all-datatypes.xml (Apache PLC4X v1.0.0, commit ea229918), following modbus.mspec; Stonecrab's codec is not involved, and a test re-runs the adapter and compares this file byte for byte.
# Transaction 1, protocol id 0, length 15 (unit id plus 14 PDU bytes), unit id 1. Function 0x10 (write multiple registers) request: start 27, quantity 4, byte count 8.
00 01 00 00 00 0F 01 10 00 1B 00 04 08 40 05 BF 0A 8B 14 5F CF
